  "_": "The basin pages the storm pipeline (tools/make_tc_basin.py, tools/storm_basin.mjs, tools/storm_fit.mjs --basin) works on. prefix: the data files (data/generated/<prefix>-*.json, the Atlantic's are unprefixed: data.json); page: the built simulator (dist/); hemisphere: the half of the page that is the basin (the pages' boxes reach across the equator for context: the East Pacific page holds the South Pacific cyclones east of the date line, which are the South Pacific page's); frame: the longitude convention of the page (180: -180..180, 360: 0..360); seasonMonth: the month a season starts in (0 January, 6 July); start: [month, day] the lab's season begins on; grid: the 5-degree (2.5 for the small basins) node grid of the maps (nx x ny nodes from lon0, lat0); ensoMonths: the months of the Nino 3.4 index the season's activity is compared with (month numbers 1-12, 13+ belong to the next calendar year); years: the first and last season of the normals (a season is named for the year it starts in); genesisYears / driftYears: the seasons the genesis maps and the drift maps are made from.",
